findings.body:
Any authenticated caller can pass `accountId` in the JSON body and read that account. The comment says this is for support staff, but there is no role, permission, or staff check before using the client-supplied id — only `auth(req)`.

**Failure mode:** A request with body `{"accountId":"victim-id"}` returns the victim account JSON for a normal user session.

Gate explicit-id lookup on a verified staff/support principal (or a separate staff-only route). Non-privileged callers must keep resolving solely to `caller.accountId`.

```suggestion
  const body = await req.json().catch(() => ({}));
  const requestedId = typeof body.accountId === "string" ? body.accountId : undefined;
  if (requestedId !== undefined && !caller.isSupportStaff) {
    return Response.json({ error: "forbidden" }, { status: 403 });
  }
  const id: string = requestedId ?? caller.accountId;
```

(Adapt `caller.isSupportStaff` to whatever auth model this codebase uses.)
